Package: devjam-science-titta-demo-analyses
Version: 1.0-2
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: devjam-tools, python3, python3-numpy, python3-pandas, python3-pil, python3-matplotlib, python3-h5py, python3-tables, python3-opencv, python3-i2mc
Recommends: xdg-user-dirs, curl, libnotify-bin
Suggests: python3-titta
Maintainer: Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>
Description: Titta demo analyses for eye-tracking data, copied to the Desktop
 The demo_analyses folder of Titta (Tobii eye-tracker toolbox), from the
 staging branch of github.com/dev-jam/Titta: trial extraction, data
 quality, fixation detection with I2MC, mapping fixations to AOIs with
 cumulative plots, scanpaths, heatmaps and gaze videos, plus
 run_analysis.py to run all steps in one go.
 .
 The scripts are installed in /usr/share/titta-demo-analyses and copied
 once per user to the Desktop (folder titta_demo_analyses, via
 devjam-run-once), where they can be edited and run. The menu entry
 "Titta demo analyses" makes a new copy; its action "Download latest
 version from GitHub" fetches the current staging branch instead.
 Existing folders are never overwritten. The exact commit of the
 packaged version is in the file VERSION.
